   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz9E6",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "It's plain and simple really; climate change, rising living costs, and economic stagnation don't exactly paint a bright picture.  To me, the Alliance Party is a genuine alternative to the status quo. We have a bold and unique vision for Aotearoa – one built around full employment, universal public services, public ownership, strong communities, and an economy that works for working people.   I want to build a future worth believing in."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz9GH",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "Growing up in Highbury, studying at Massey, and working two part-time jobs, I understand the challenges facing ordinary people and young people today. My experience in unions, climate activism, and community work has shaped my belief that we can build a better future. I want to bring a fresh perspective, strong principles, and a bold vision for Aotearoa to politics."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz9IS",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Building a future worth believing in."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz9Kd",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Creating good jobs and a productive economy through a renewed Ministry of Works (KiwiWorks)."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz9Mo",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Expanding public housing, strengthening tenants rights and treating housing as a human right."
     }
    ],
